{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up","id":1171765,"title":"How The Heck Does This Setting Hold Up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-30T04:50:14-08:00","id":1171765,"title":"How The Heck Does This Setting Hold Up?","content":"First of all, let me start by saying that I know almost nothing about classic Mage, aside from the fact the Technocracy rewrote reality so that mortals stopped believing in the supernatural. And this apparently had an impact on the way magic worked, and pretty much screwed the Fae over pretty hard.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what about the other splats? If mages and Changelings are having such a rough time of getting things to work for them, then why aren't Werewolves, Vampires, Ghosts and the like seeing a decline in their power, or even fading from existence? Tremere mages don't seem to have a problem, and even came up with a new type of magic when they lost access to their old ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> And what would happen if the Masquerade (I'm using that as a blanket term, by the way) were to be broken and existence of the supernatural was revealed to the world? Would the Technocracy's magic be undone by this revelation, or would it somehow find a way to reinstate itself, despite hard evidence to the contrary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T05:45:41-08:00","id":1171774,"title":"","content":"&quot;First of all, let me start by saying that I know almost nothing about classic Mage...&quot;<br /> <br /> I can tell. All your questions are simply answered by reading the book. Just pick up a copy, any edition will do, and give it a thorough read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T08:18:34-08:00","id":1171793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up#post1171765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> why aren't Werewolves, Vampires, Ghosts and the like seeing a decline in their power, or even fading from existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely, they ARE. blood is spreading thin, the war is raging ever harder, the fera are dying off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T09:00:31-08:00","id":1171802,"title":"","content":"There are some things that are part of the Tapestry intrinsically bound to the Rules of Reality, this is known primarily as Static Magic and is where Werewolves, Vampires, Sorceres and so forth occupy in the cosmology mythos of Mage the Ascension. The Consensus is a powerful thing dictating the flow of 'mundane reality' but there are still things that it doesn't get to out right change. Mages use True Magick however which instead of employing the little static laws that let other supernaturals do their thing they use secrets of Reality itself to reshape the tapestry to their whim, they literally remake the world as they see fit when they perform an act of magic, no matter how small. Changelings likewise occupy a special place as they do not remake reality so much as use the power of dreams given power and form and so suffer from the active disbelief in magic in that it makes Arts harder to perform. However because a Changeling isn't rewriting the Tapestry but actually sidestepping it whatever they do doesn't have consequences for the caster like it may for a Mage as the tapestry likes being a certain way and the snap back of meddling with it is known as Paradox which any Mage may suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T09:12:35-08:00","id":1171805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1171793#post1171793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Largely, they ARE. blood is spreading thin, the war is raging ever harder, the fera are dying off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The blood is thinning because Caine cursed the lower generations. Not because of anything the Age of Reason did to them. And it only continues to thin with subsequent generations. I've also heard something about how the blood thickens with age or something to that effect. So vampires grow more powerful over time.<br /> <br /> And if the war is raging harder, that sounds like the things in Werewolf are becoming more powerful, not less. How come the spirits of faeries started dropping like flies, but the spirits of Gaia only got pissed off?<br /> <br /> And none of this answers the question of what would happen if the masquerade were broken. It only took watching the moon landing for us to bring back the Fae.<br /> <br /> What if millions of people saw a video or a broadcast that showed the existence of monsters and there was no way to cover it up? Suddenly, the world understands that vampires are real, ghosts are real, werewolves are real, <i>magic is real.</i><br /> <br /> What happens to the Age of Reason when that occurs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-30-2017, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T09:50:14-08:00","id":1171815,"title":"","content":"The world is decaying. The explanations splat by splat don't need to communicate. <br /> The blood is thinking because of the curse. The blood is thinning because it can't exist. <br /> The bloid is thinning because they are being culled. <br /> <br /> Three explanations, all valid. <br /> <br /> And what would happen if these veils and masquerades broke? Less than you might be thinking. Consider the big mage explanation for something not evoking paradox is it being sufficiently accepted by a consensus. <br /> <br /> So, to mage, people on some level believe in monsters. That's all. <br /> <br /> <br /> You also overestimate the human resiliency. The War of the Worlds fundamentally altered human perception of reality... but it didn't last.<br /> The cold war made definite changes... over the course of decades. <br /> The renaissance changed our world view forever... through centuries of effort paying off and taking root.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T10:34:30-08:00","id":1171827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1171815#post1171815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to mage, people on some level believe in monsters. That's all.<br /> <br /> <br /> You also overestimate the human resiliency. The War of the Worlds fundamentally altered human perception of reality... but it didn't last.<br /> The cold war made definite changes... over the course of decades.<br /> The renaissance changed our world view forever... through centuries of effort paying off and taking root.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the thing. From what I've been lead to understand, the technocracy hoped to stamp out these supernatural threats plaguing humans by making them think they didn't exist. So for them to come out and prove that they do exist would have to have some kind of dramatic effect. Unless they're willing to conduct some other massive, reality warping ritual to make everybody forget about them again, the world would become aware of the existence of supernatural beings and powers. Which, according to consensus, means these creatures would return to power as more folks started to believe in them again, and had hard proof of their existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Banality would do a complete 180 as mortals exposed to the truth started to wonder about other possibilities being kept hidden from them. As I said before, it only took the moon landing (something which wasn't even supernatural) being publicly broadcast in order to flood the world with enough Glamour for the Sidhe to make a comeback. So if you broadcast people changing into giant animals, sprinting at 100 miles per hour, levitating garbage trucks with their minds, or summoning a plague of rats to come pouring into the city streets.<br /> <br /> That's not something the world just looks at and thinks<i> &quot;Oh, that's cool... Okay, what are we having for dinner tonight?&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-30-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T11:50:43-08:00","id":1171841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up#post1171765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, let me start by saying that I know almost nothing about classic Mage, aside from the fact the Technocracy rewrote reality so that mortals stopped believing in the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I'm going to go back to address this, because it's incorrect and that's a big disconnect here.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy didn't &quot;rewrite&quot; anything. The Order of Reason (the precursor to the Technocracy, as the Technocratic Union is actually under 200 years old) made massive strides in understanding the way the world really worked (that is, reality is subjective and dominant 'truths' are based on observer consensus), and then set out to make the world work better for humanity by getting humans to see the world in a fashion that benefits them. The OoR's tools were rational thought, science, philosophy, and education, which took away special knowledge from those hording it. You don't need a priest to cast out a demon, you need a doctor to heal your sickness, and anyone could study medicine without needing to jump through a faith's loops.<br /> <br /> Of course, mages are humans in many ways, and the altruistic intentions quickly bent from empowering human creativity to control. The OoR realized that they could eventually be superceded by the masses as they used the masses to push back at other mages (and supernaturals). So the OoR's more ambitious and power hungry members started taking control from the idealists (with multiple purges). Knowing the reality is ultimately subjective, the leaders of the OoR subverted their initial goals. They wrote rules for reality, and used their positions of influence over Sleeper thinkers to get them to &quot;discover&quot; those rules as parts of science and rational thought. As that made their Sleeper followers more technologically power, it also made the belief in what the OoR wanted to be truth stronger.<br /> <br /> At first, this actually 'broke' reality (this would be the Sorcerer's Crusade era) into major Reality Zones. What was true varied wildly based on location. The OoR pushed for expansion and control (influencing the Age of Exploration and the expansion of European colonialism) to unify these Zones, and large succeeded over a very long time. Eventually, during the Victorian era, is when they reorganized as the Technocracy with the backers of the British Empire seeing the global unity possible as they abandoned the last vestiges of the OoR's original mission.<br /> <br /> So, the Union never rewrote reality. They wrote their own rules for reality, and got people to believe in them. One of the Union's biggest problems though, is that humans are very capable of holding contradictory beliefs. Simply giving them new things to believe didn't get them to stop having old beliefs; even if those old beliefs aren't to any obvious benefit. The modern Consensus reality they created is imperfect because despite all their efforts to address this, it remains the case. The old realities still exist in that Consensus. Making one reality the strongest, didn't make it the only one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:38:44-08:00","id":1171860,"title":"","content":"A lot of what keeps supernatural stuff running the World of Darkness, despite the Consensus, is Inertia. The Consensus allows hedge wizards to use Sorcery Paths, even according to ancient ways, because the Consensus has <i>always</i> allowed them. It's deeply ingrained in the fabric of human belief, so an individual can still use them. The Mythic Threads exist because, even if people wouldn't seriously say that magic or ghosts or monsters are real, those things still have a hold on our collective imaginations. A part of humans has always maintained, &quot;Magic and monsters aren't real...but....what if...?&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if we assume the Consensus doesn't support certain things, there are explanations given in the Mage books (like the Revised Storyteller's Handbook and others) for why vampires and werewolves et al are still around. For Vampires, mages assume that they WOULD be too Vulgar to exist...which is why they have to drink blood. Blood is the Life. It is the currency of the soul. And it carries mystic power. Specifically, vampires are able to derive Quintessence from blood - siphoning the energy that underpins a creature's existence to prop up its own. In the same way that other Bygones feed on Quintessence to remain in the mortal realm - like by sitting around a Node or entering into a pact with a mage as a Familiar - so too do vampires have their own form of Thaumivore lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Moreover, again, vampires are old beings. Their curse is ancient, and allegedly placed by God. If anyone's Will outranks that of the Consensus, it would be the Most High. Vampires continue to exist because a power higher than mere human belief proclaims as much.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to Werewolves, who are even more secure in their existence. The Fera have supposedly been around for millions of years. Additionally, shapeshifters aren't just biological beings. They are half-spirit. And one of the consistent details in the Mage cosmology is that spirits are unaffected by the whims of the Consensus. They just ARE. Spirit Charms never suffer Paradox, and may enter the material world and manifest physically at their choice, so long as they are individually powerful enough to do so. This is probably because spirits are the mechanisms behind Reality, and are inextricably tied to it. Shifters, being half spirit, share this innate tie to the essential flow of existence, and are therefore afforded broad tolerance by the Consensus in what they can do. Hell, the one way they seem to be at odds with human belief - the Delirium that panics and memory-alters people who see shifters in their full supernatural glory - is explicitly stated in Werewolf as having more to do with Humanity's deep, racial fear of shifters, and not Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:42:34-08:00","id":1171862,"title":"","content":"Wraiths, meanwhile, are largely unconcerned with the Consensus (and vice versa), since they are ephemeral beings by default. They don't exist on the Material side of the Shroud, so their presence isn't a problem. And they fuel their ghostly powers - which could affect the living world, true - with Pathos, energy taken from human passions. One could easily argue that wraiths, too, take Quintessence from humans, in this case in the form of emotional energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:58:13-08:00","id":1171884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1171841#post1171841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, I'm going to go back to address this, because it's incorrect and that's a big disconnect here.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy didn't &quot;rewrite&quot; anything. The Order of Reason (the precursor to the Technocracy, as the Technocratic Union is actually under 200 years old) made massive strides in understanding the way the world really worked (that is, reality is subjective and dominant 'truths' are based on observer consensus), and then set out to make the world work better for humanity by getting humans to see the world in a fashion that benefits them. The OoR's tools were rational thought, science, philosophy, and education, which took away special knowledge from those hording it. You don't need a priest to cast out a demon, you need a doctor to heal your sickness, and anyone could study medicine without needing to jump through a faith's loops.<br /> <br /> Of course, mages are humans in many ways, and the altruistic intentions quickly bent from empowering human creativity to control. The OoR realized that they could eventually be superceded by the masses as they used the masses to push back at other mages (and supernaturals). So the OoR's more ambitious and power hungry members started taking control from the idealists (with multiple purges). Knowing the reality is ultimately subjective, the leaders of the OoR subverted their initial goals. They wrote rules for reality, and used their positions of influence over Sleeper thinkers to get them to &quot;discover&quot; those rules as parts of science and rational thought. As that made their Sleeper followers more technologically power, it also made the belief in what the OoR wanted to be truth stronger.<br /> <br /> At first, this actually 'broke' reality (this would be the Sorcerer's Crusade era) into major Reality Zones. What was true varied wildly based on location. The OoR pushed for expansion and control (influencing the Age of Exploration and the expansion of European colonialism) to unify these Zones, and large succeeded over a very long time. Eventually, during the Victorian era, is when they reorganized as the Technocracy with the backers of the British Empire seeing the global unity possible as they abandoned the last vestiges of the OoR's original mission.<br /> <br /> So, the Union never rewrote reality. They wrote their own rules for reality, and got people to believe in them. One of the Union's biggest problems though, is that humans are very capable of holding contradictory beliefs. Simply giving them new things to believe didn't get them to stop having old beliefs; even if those old beliefs aren't to any obvious benefit. The modern Consensus reality they created is imperfect because despite all their efforts to address this, it remains the case. The old realities still exist in that Consensus. Making one reality the strongest, didn't make it the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for explaining it in more detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T14:23:36-08:00","id":1172385,"title":"","content":"Mage is an awesome game;, great for fantasy-games; I've never ran a cannon MtA game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T15:02:50-08:00","id":1172397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1172385#post1172385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is an awesome game;, great for fantasy-games; I've never ran a cannon MtA game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you run a trebuchet MtA game, at least?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:56:16-07:00","id":1204516,"title":"","content":"Fae are sensitive to belief. That is a big deal with them. Even in the Dark Ages they were super duper vulnerable to certain acts and objects, in part because of the faith behind them. Furthermore, Fae are weak to the Banal. The normal, the organized, the regimented. The industrial revolution nearly wiped them out, and cut off Arcadia from our world.<br /> <br /> Vampires are just blood-sucking reality deviants. Whether you believe in Ventrue Methesulahs or not, one still owns your company and could make you disappear if he wanted to. The most your faith will do to him is make him take a few steps back, if you're one of the tiny % of people who have powerful Faith in the modern age.<br /> <br /> So if you actually read Changeling, or Mage, you'll see why the Technocracy and the Order of Reason's actions have hurt some supernatural beings and not others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:36:57-07:00","id":1204540,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Consensus was changing well before even the Craftmasons, the group of Enlightened Philosopher-scientists that were the major force behind the creation of the Order of Reason. The Fae have already been mentioned but there were also fall of House Tremere into Clan Tremere, specifically the reason the Tremere turned themselves into vampires. They found their Magic becoming harder to preform and feared the loss of their powers and Magic-based immortality/longevity, they didn't understand that the Consensus was changing. So they eventually hit on the idea of becoming vampires to preserve what they could.<br /> <br /> To throw all the changing of the Consensus at the hands of the Order of Reason and Technocracy is an oversimplification of things. Certainly, they ensured it would go down the path it did and likely sped it up but it was still changing regardless.<br /> <br /> And it's also worth noting that even despite everything that's happened to the world and the Consensus, it's not all doom and gloom for everyone that's not a Technocrat. Or that the Union or Science itself is some Wonder crushing, Banality generating monstrosity that will stamp out creativity and Wonder. Indeed, the Changelings, one of groups hit the hardest by the growth of Science received a large boost from the Space Race and Moon Landings to the point that group of Fae that had long abandoned Earth, returned. All because of sheer Wonder produced by the Masses looking up into space and dreaming of going there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:54:15-07:00","id":1204567,"title":"","content":"The only thing that really doesn't work about Mage is the idea that the Technocrats are winning. In the real world, 84 percent of the population is religious. The Technocratic paradigm can't even win in a universe where it's right, but somehow it kicked all kinds of ass in a universe where it's wrong? Nonsense.<br /> <br /> If anything, the game feels like it was constructed by the kind of paranoid people who think there is some kind of war on Christmas because a tiny, powerless handful of atheists complain about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-08-2018, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:04:51-07:00","id":1204574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204567#post1204567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that really doesn't work about Mage is the idea that the Technocrats are winning. In the real world, 84 percent of the population is religious. The Technocratic paradigm can't even win in a universe where it's right, but somehow it kicked all kinds of ass in a universe where it's wrong? Nonsense.<br /> <br /> If anything, the game feels like it was constructed by the kind of paranoid people who think there is some kind of war on Christmas because a tiny, powerless handful of atheists complain about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's true, come to think of it. Billions of Christians, Jews, Muslims, Hindus, Shintoists, Buddhists, and whatever other religion you feel like throwing in there still exist in the modern age and have very devout followers. How exactly did the Technocracy become so well established if this is meant to take place in a similarly developed world?<br /> <br /> Historically speaking, religious communities were violently suppressing the more scientific communities.<br /> <br /> Those who studied science were forced to do so in secret, for fear of being persecuted as a heretic.<br /> <br /> And anybody claiming that some brilliant men of history were religious or at the very least agnostic, keep in mind that they lived in an age where saying that your gods were a lie would get you tied to a stake and burned in front of a live studio audience. You really think these brilliant scholars were foolish enough to come right out and claim they were atheists, knowing it would get them killed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:09:03-07:00","id":1204576,"title":"","content":"Of course, the reason it works emotionally is precisely because it is realistically absurd. It plays on the fear that someone is going to barge in and smash your Wiccan stuff or your Christian church or whatever. And since huge numbers of people feel that fear, despite us scientifically minded atheists being a tiny, powerless minority, the audience eats it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:17:29-07:00","id":1204582,"title":"","content":"Actually, M20 acknowledges that the notion that the Technocracy is winning is absurd, and that it's absurd because so much of the world still believes in magic. It's only in the West that the Technocracy can be said to be winning; and even that's up for debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:53:20-07:00","id":1204598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204582#post1204582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, M20 acknowledges that the notion that the Technocracy is winning is absurd, and that it's absurd because so much of the world still believes in magic. It's only in the West that the Technocracy can be said to be winning; and even that's up for debate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's good to know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:08:33-07:00","id":1204868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204582#post1204582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, M20 acknowledges that the notion that the Technocracy is winning is absurd, and that it's absurd because so much of the world still believes in magic. It's only in the West that the Technocracy can be said to be winning; and even that's up for debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. However, I want to adress one fact:<br /> <br /> In the real world we see that even the people who believe in magic use technological apparatuses. And in the WoD, even the likes of vampires and mystic mages use them :P . That sustains the Belief in technology and keeps science (or rather it's consequences) as a valid and strong Paradigm nearly everywhere.<br /> <br /> Buddhists may believe that space it's an illusion and thus a few enlightened can teleport, but most preffer to use taxicabs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:28:54-07:00","id":1204902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204868#post1204868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. However, I want to adress one fact:<br /> <br /> In the real world we see that even the people who believe in magic use technological apparatuses. And in the WoD, even the likes of vampires and mystic mages use them :P . That sustains the Belief in technology and keeps science (or rather it's consequences) as a valid and strong Paradigm nearly everywhere.<br /> <br /> Buddhists may believe that space it's an illusion and thus a few enlightened can teleport, but most preffer to use taxicabs</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that such things would never have gotten established in a metaphysically idealistic universe. Even in the real world, people have to be dragged kicking and screaming into believing in science, and we live in a world where science is objectively correct. Even then, people only believe in the bare minimum of science needed to function. Anything they can get away with believing is God or some other superstition like horoscopes, they will cling right onto. So in a metaphysically idealistic world, religion and superstition would be fact, and any attempt to contradict it would never have gotten off the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:32:49-07:00","id":1204905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204868#post1204868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. However, I want to adress one fact:<br /> <br /> In the real world we see that even the people who believe in magic use technological apparatuses. And in the WoD, even the likes of vampires and mystic mages use them :P . That sustains the Belief in technology and keeps science (or rather it's consequences) as a valid and strong Paradigm nearly everywhere.<br /> <br /> Buddhists may believe that space it's an illusion and thus a few enlightened can teleport, but most preffer to use taxicabs</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know about you guys, but most forms of electronics may as well be magic for me. I mean, look at a motherboard some time. This piece of green silicon with bits of metal spot welded onto it is somehow responsible for my computer functioning properly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2018, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T11:01:31-07:00","id":1204914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204905#post1204905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know about you guys, but most forms of electronics may as well be magic for me. I mean, look at at a motherboard some time. This piece of green silicon with bits of metal spot welded onto it is somehow responsible for my computer functioning properly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. And yet you're still using them. The Consensus does not care about the underlying principles, only about things that people can see - hence why Perception enhancing it's always Coincident unless you use it on another person. Sure, &quot;people can't see auras&quot;(except when they can), but as long as only you (or other peple that believes in Auras or that can rationalize such sight somehow) know where you get your information, the Consensus doesn't care<br /> <br /> Unless you're using your psionic powers to writte your messages in this medium, you're empowering Technocracy (and VA) tech. Heck, if you're chaneling your psionic powers trough a computer you're empowering them too - it has to be obvious that you don't need the cristal box in order to get out from their Consensus. (Let's not get into the detail that psionics it's actually a practice under the Technocracy)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that such things would never have gotten established in a metaphysically idealistic universe. Even in the real world, people have to be dragged kicking and screaming into believing in science, and we live in a world where science is objectively correct. Even then, people only believe in the bare minimum of science needed to function. Anything they can get away with believing is God or some other superstition like horoscopes, they will cling right onto. So in a metaphysically idealistic world, religion and superstition would be fact, and any attempt to contradict it would never have gotten off the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's coming from a very exeptical school of tought that assumes magic isn't real and only then tries to apply that logic on another world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . In the real world people isn't able to do magick because they &quot;aren't enlightened enough&quot;, &quot;don't have enough faith (to walk on water)&quot;, &quot;totally can but not on presence of unbelievers&quot;.<br /> Or so they say.<br /> <br /> Mage neatly states that one of the greatest failures of the antecesors of the Traditions was that they deviced magick to be hard, something that only the Initiate would understand. You need to be a saint, a learned mage, or an enlightened monk to benefit from it (in other words, you have to be the kind of people that can? do magic in the real world). You can totaly move mountains if you have enough Merit.<br /> Since most people isn't that Elite, then superstition being fact in WoD (and it still is because Sorcery exists) doesn't mean that they won't use technology anyway. And that's all you need to establish a Paradigm - the Technocracy won over with sweet deals, they weren't able to erode faith in superstition like they wanted to do, but they did establish technology &quot;milacres&quot; even among people that would refuse to believe in causality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2018, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T11:55:07-07:00","id":1204930,"title":"","content":"No. People constantly believe that God cured their cancer, even when they just got lucky. People believe their horoscopes worked out, again when they just got lucky. People believe all sorts of little good luck charms and good luck behaviors work, even in a universe where it's just that a certain percentage of people will statistically succeed. This idea that they used to believe only saints or whoever could work magic is something White Wolf straight up pulled out of their rears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T12:22:13-07:00","id":1204940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204930#post1204930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. People constantly believe that God cured their cancer, even when they just got lucky. People believe their horoscopes worked out, again when they just got lucky. People believe all sorts of little good luck charms and good luck behaviors work, even in a universe where it's just that a certain percentage of people will statistically succeed. This idea that they used to believe only saints or whoever could work magic is something White Wolf straight up pulled out of their rears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't avidly follow horoscopes, but I've noticed that mine are usually pretty accurate whenever I do check up on them.<br /> <br /> Awful lot of 'coincidences' happening there for me to wave it off as superstition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And now that I think about it, even if we assume that the Technocracy did manage to crush the more pagan mages over the centuries, our real world modernity would have given them ample chance to recover. It's no longer acceptable to hunt down and kill people because of their religious or cultural beliefs. Hell, even Satanists are allowed to walk around in the open without fear of being put on trial simply for practicing devil worship.<br /> <br /> <br /> By suppressing people's belief in the supernatural, the Technocracy has ironically enabled them to walk around in the open. Who cares if your neighbor is trying to summon a demon in their basement under the light of a full moon? If demons don't actually exist, then you've got nothing to worry about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hey, what smells like sulfur and burning flesh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2018, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T13:13:09-07:00","id":1204956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204940#post1204940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't avidly follow horoscopes, but I've noticed that mine are usually pretty accurate whenever I do check up on them.<br /> <br /> Awful lot of 'coincidences' happening there for me to wave it off as superstition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's because humans are terrible at understanding how true randomness works. It's pretty counter-intuitive for people think about daily life, but lots of coincidences are proof of a truly random system. A coin flip cannot be truly random if it was impossible to get it to flip heads 30 times in a row for example.<br /> <br /> We are geared up to spot patterns and to consider recurring patterns as important and worthy of reverence, regardless of their source. It doesn't matter at all why the pattern has came about, we just care that it's there, we'll think up a reason why later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:29:30-07:00","id":1205022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1204930#post1204930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. People constantly believe that God cured their cancer, even when they just got lucky. People believe their horoscopes worked out, again when they just got lucky. People believe <b>all sorts of <span style=\"font-size:16px\">little</span> good luck charms and good luck behaviors work</b>, even in a universe where it's just that a certain percentage of people will statistically succeed. This idea that they used to believe only saints or whoever could work magic is something White Wolf straight up pulled out of their rears.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it just happens that little good luck charms and good luck behaviours are always Coincident.<br /> <br /> <i>When did I mentioned little good luck charms as the kind of magic that only saints can do?</i>. I explicitly mentioned transport, moving mountains, walking over water<b>. Do that seems like little good luck charms to you, or more like the stuff reputedly SAINTS can do</b>.<br /> <br /> You don't use a charm to travel to another country at great speeds, and you certainly don't pray for the mountains to come to your house because you're too weak to travel yourself! Nobody does that, not even people that believe 100% that these milacres are possible in the real world. All that people does it's to get a little good luck with prayers so the plane doesn't fall. And that's perfectly acceptable under the Consensus in WoD, as far as we know it may even work. <hr /><br /> I didn't wanted to mention medicine because medicine it's far from an exact science and even in the real world there's lots and lots of stories of witches healing people that science couldn't cure. Stories that, I imagine, are true in WoD (if not in real life). People pray to get better and it works so many times in the real world that scientists study the effect of &quot;suggestion&quot; and &quot;placebo&quot;. Which basically means healing because you believed you would. You will never know what cured your Cancer because medicine doesn't cure it reliably either.<br /> <br /> However, believing after the fact that it was God doesn't undermine Technocratical Paradigm - you need to be way more hard core than that if you want to trully anger the Progenitors. Like those people that would refuse to take medicine because God is going to heal them, which presumes God will help you if you don't help yourself. Medics were a thing before Christianity, you know, people went to medics in ancient times too, and they weren't asked to leave their beliefs in the door.<br /> <br /> Now, in my country there was a priest that was reputed to be able to cure cancer. And guess what?, chrsitians didn't tought that such feat was the most common thing in the world and went with their lives like nothing. He got immensely famous. He got immensely famous because people that can cure with God (as opposite as merely being cured by God) it's VERY impressive, not every tom in the farm it's supposed to be able to do that.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I don't see the impossibility of beliving in science here because medics were working their mojo far before the Order of Reason was ever founded and religion can explain why they work (medics work because they are intermediaries of the divine).That's why, I believe, so many religious people go to the doctor to be healed by God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now that I think about it, even if we assume that the Technocracy did manage to crush the more pagan mages over the centuries, our real world modernity would have given them ample chance to recover. It's no longer acceptable to hunt down and kill people because of their religious or cultural beliefs. Hell, even Satanists are allowed to walk around in the open without fear of being put on trial simply for practicing devil worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true, and that's where M20 assertion: That the Technocracy failed in crushing the more pagan mages, trully shines.<br /> <br /> Multiculturalism was always in the agenda of the Traditions, and it would seem that they managed to push it trough. Albeit in doing so they had to accept that the Syndicate can foster &quot;light&quot; and &quot;safe&quot; versions of their ancient practices, arguably poisoning their venerable waters with angsty new-agers that are eager to believe in &quot;little good luck charms&quot; but would pale in the face of dragons. Oh well, I still think that the Traditions managed a victory there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By suppressing people's belief in the supernatural, the Technocracy has ironically enabled them to walk around in the open. Who cares if your neighbor is trying to summon a demon in their basement under the light of a full moon? If demons don't actually exist, then you've got nothing to worry about. </div> </div> </div>If nobody cares about demon sumoning because it doesn't exist then your neighbor it's going to need a Sanctum to summon a demon Coincidentally. In Cruzade summoning demons wasn't just Coincident, it was Consensual. You could do it w/o magick nor Sorcery. I'm not sure if that's still possible in the modern era, but it could be. After all, WoD it's a very shitty place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-09-2018, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:57:19-07:00","id":1205029,"title":"","content":"That's not because it is intrinsic to the Christian paradigm that only saints can do it. Rather, it's because miracles never ever ever happen in real life. So stories of miracles are always about how they heard from somebody who heard it from somebody else. And so spectacular feats gradually became associated with remarkable individuals whom you've never personally met. In a world where the Christian paradigm was real, that's simply not how history would unfold. People would believe that there prayers are answered, because they would be. And what those prayers can accomplish would spiral upwards as each miracle reinforced belief in the power of prayer, until people are praying themselves up mansions and teleporting where they need to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:51:05-07:00","id":1205289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> stories of miracles are always about how they heard from somebody who heard it from somebody else. </div> </div> </div>Not really, there are many documented cases of milacres. It just happens that it's impossible to demonstrate the divine source of those milacres<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1171765-how-the-heck-does-this-setting-hold-up?p=1205029#post1205029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not because it is intrinsic to the Christian paradigm that only saints can do it. Rather, it's because miracles never ever ever happen in real life. So stories of miracles are always about how they heard from somebody who heard it from somebody else. And so spectacular feats gradually became associated with remarkable individuals whom you've never personally met. In a world where the Christian paradigm was real, that's simply not how history would unfold. People would believe that there prayers are answered, because they would be. And what those prayers can accomplish would spiral upwards as each miracle reinforced belief in the power of prayer, until people are praying themselves up mansions and teleporting where they need to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believers in the real world don't think &quot;Oh well, my prayer was unheard because milacres can't happen in real life anyway&quot;. Faith does explain why milacres are rare.<br /> <br /> Remember that in the Bible, when Jesus ask one of his apostol to walk over water he falters and fails. A frigging Apostol almost got it, but still failed in the end. There's such things as tests of faith and these are supposed to be difficult.<br /> The man who was able to move a mountain with Faith was the same man who plucked out his own eye because that eye had dared to tempt him. Anyone can use Faith to do anything, but not everyone has so much Faith.<br /> <br /> The frailty and weakness of human being it's one of the fundaments of Christianity, praying and not getting a milacre isn't &quot;proof that Faith it's wrong&quot; because <u>Faith never assumes prayers are always answered.</u> People has never believed that, one must think ancent people were <i>very </i>stupid to think otherwise. People go to preachers and priests when they're haunted by a demon (or stuff like that) because they believe that these special and dedicated persons have more God in them than themselves or some other kind of investiture that sets them appart. And even among preachers there are those with more and less faith.<br /> <br /> I think you're arguing that stating that a prayer didn't caused the miracle because the faith of the individual faltered it's an post-hock argument that only can be rational in a world where Faith Doesn't Work. That's why I say that you come from a very exeptic mentality that doesn't translate well to a magical universe. Such perspective assumes magick has to be fair and work consistently like it was science, but magick hasn't to be fair nor act in a predictable fashion. A world where magic it's real it's not necessarily a world where magick it's a science. From a Paradigm that does believe in magick, these aren't convinient arguments to disregard failure but the way things are supposed to work and have always worked.<br /> <br /> Thus, in a world where Christian Paradigm was real people would still be weak, prayers would still go unanswered, and the road of faith would be hard because it was always assumed to be hard-because that's how old mystics encoded it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-10-2018, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}